// Lets the server restart and stop the machine it runs on.
//
// Owner, 2026-09-25: "Auch reboot Shutdown auf dem Systemdisplay funktionieren
// nicht" — the buttons reached the server, the server ran `systemctl reboot`,
// and the machine refused it with exit status 1.
//
// `crates/ovs-core/src/power.rs` says of exactly this: "A server running as an
// unprivileged user cannot reboot the machine unless it has been given
// permission to, and that is a deployment decision rather than something to work
// around." This file is that decision. It was never made, so the buttons could
// not work on any machine.
//
// # Why polkit and not a capability
//
// `CAP_SYS_BOOT` would let the process call the kernel directly, which is faster
// and loses whatever has not reached the disk. The server asks the init system
// instead, on purpose: the show is written down, the database is closed, and the
// units come down in the order they were brought up. Asking logind is a D-Bus
// call, and what decides whether a D-Bus call is allowed is polkit.
//
// # What it grants, and what it does not
//
// Restart and power off, for the one system user the core runs as. Both the
// plain actions and the `-multiple-sessions` ones, because a machine with
// somebody logged in at the console is the ordinary case in a rack room and a
// button that works only when nobody is there is not a button.
//
// **Not the `-ignore-inhibit` variants.** An inhibitor is something that has
// asked to be allowed to finish — an update, a write — and `systemctl reboot`
// respects one unless told otherwise. Granting those here would quietly override
// every inhibitor on the machine, which is a different and much larger
// permission than the one the buttons need.
//
// Not halt either. Nothing offers it, and a permission nothing uses is one
// nobody reviews.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
  if (subject.user !== "ovs") {
    return undefined;
  }

  if (
    action.id === "org.freedesktop.login1.reboot" ||
    action.id === "org.freedesktop.login1.reboot-multiple-sessions" ||
    action.id === "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off" ||
    action.id === "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off-multiple-sessions"
  ) {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
  }

  // Everything else this user might ask for is somebody else's decision.
  return undefined;
});
